# Real gap found and fixed during Docker verification (Part D, production
# engineering completion pass): this file did not exist at all before now.
# Every docker-compose service (api/worker/web) uses `context: ..` (the
# repo root), so without this, `COPY apps/api/ ./` / `COPY apps/web/ ./`
# would copy apps/api/.env - a real file containing real secrets (a
# Hugging Face token, a Groq API key) - directly into image layers, which
# can persist even if a later layer "deletes" it. See
# docs/DECISIONS/0015-docker-verification.md.

# Secrets - never baked into an image. Real config comes from env_file/
# environment at container *run* time (docker-compose.full.yml), never
# copied in at *build* time.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Python virtual environments and caches - large, host-specific, and the
# image installs its own dependencies fresh via `pip install -e .`.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# Frontend build artifacts/dependencies - the image runs its own `npm install`.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# Local runtime state - real user data/uploads from local dev, and MLflow
# tracking data - neither belongs in an image.
apps/api/.data/
mlruns/

# Version control / editor / OS noise.
.git/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store

# Large raw ML data this project explicitly keeps out of version control
# too (see ml/datasets/README.md) - never needed inside a runtime image.
ml/datasets/manifests/
